# Error Recovery & Fault Confinement State Machine Diagram

`can-logger-decoder` v2.0.0 · Day 3 Architecture Specifications

This diagram models the ISO 11898-1 fault confinement and bus-off recovery
state machine implemented in `src/state/error_machine.c` and
`src/state/bus_off_recovery.c`.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NORMAL

    NORMAL --> WARNING   : TEC/REC >= 96
    WARNING --> ERROR_PASSIVE : TEC/REC >= 127
    ERROR_PASSIVE --> BUS_OFF : TEC > 255

    BUS_OFF --> RECOVERING : 128 occurrences of 11 recessive bits (ISO 11898-1)
    RECOVERING --> NORMAL : Recovery complete (TEC & REC reset to 0)
    BUS_OFF --> RESET : Hardware / Software SPI reset command
    RESET --> NORMAL : Reset initialized & CONFIG exit
    NORMAL --> RESET : SPI fault / manual re-init

    WARNING --> NORMAL : Error count drops < 96
    ERROR_PASSIVE --> WARNING : Error count drops < 127
    RECOVERING --> BUS_OFF : Recovery failure / bus timeout
    RESET --> FAILED : Maximum retries exceeded

    state "Bus Off Recovery Sub-Machine" as BOR {
        [*] --> IDLE
        IDLE --> WAITING_BUS_IDLE : EVT_BUS_OFF detected
        WAITING_BUS_IDLE --> RESET_ISSUED : 128 sequences elapsed
        RESET_ISSUED --> RECOVERING : Controller hardware reset
        RECOVERING --> RECOVERED : Controller entered NORMAL mode
        RECOVERED --> [*]
        RESET_ISSUED --> FAILED : Max retry limit reached (5 attempts)
        WAITING_BUS_IDLE --> FAILED : Idle detection timeout (1000 ms)
    }

    note right of NORMAL
        NORMAL (Error Active):
        Node transmits active error flags (6 dominant bits).
        TEC < 96 and REC < 96.
    end note

    note right of WARNING
        WARNING:
        Error warning limit reached.
        TEC >= 96 or REC >= 96.
    end note

    note right of ERROR_PASSIVE
        ERROR PASSIVE:
        Node transmits passive error flags (6 recessive bits).
        Must wait suspend transmission time (8 bits).
        TEC >= 127 or REC >= 127.
    end note

    note right of BUS_OFF
        BUS OFF:
        Output driver disabled, node electrically disconnected.
        TEC > 255.
    end note
```
